<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ruleset name="phlix-hub">
    <description>PSR-12 coding standard for detain/phlix-hub.</description>

    <!--
        S299 — `tests` joined this list on 2026-08-10. It had NEVER been linted:
        the ruleset named only src + scripts, and CI ran phpcs with an explicit
        PSR12 standard over src/ only, which ignores this file entirely and so
        never consulted the list below. At f4ab19f the test tree carried
        696 errors and 141 warnings across 69 of its 241 files while the
        "PHP CodeSniffer (PSR-12)" check was green on every commit.

        The standard for `tests` is deliberately IDENTICAL to `src` — no relaxed
        line length, no exemption for snake_case method names — because the
        evidence said the test tree already agreed with it: 2441 of its 3127
        methods were camelCase before S299, and every one of the 141 over-long
        lines was ordinary wrappable code, not an unbreakable fixture literal.
        A per-sniff exemption here would have enshrined the minority drift and
        silently admitted every new violation of it.

        ⚠ Do not delete a <file> entry. `scripts/assert-phpcs-corpus.php` fails
        the build when one goes missing, and asserts a floor on the number of
        files phpcs actually inspected under each — a linter that traverses
        nothing exits 0 and looks exactly like a clean run.

        S333 — the `<arg value="np"/>` flag (phpcs `-n` + `-p`) was removed on
        2026-08-20. The S299 gate runs phpcs against this ruleset file, so `-n`
        was live and suppressed 6 warnings across 5 files under scripts/.
        Warnings are gate failures per S109. `scripts/assert-phpcs-corpus.php`
        fails the build if any `<arg value>` re-introduces the `n` flag.
    -->
    <file>src</file>
    <file>scripts</file>
    <file>tests</file>

    <arg name="colors"/>
    <arg name="extensions" value="php"/>

    <rule ref="PSR12"/>
</ruleset>
